[
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://lean-lang.org/doc/api/Init/Data/Array/Subarray.html#Array.toSubarray\">Array.toSubarray</a> allows making a subarray from an array. I was wondering if there's a similar API for slicing a subarray into another subarray? (I think this would amount to changing the indices in the underlying representation)</p>",
        "id": 578006832,
        "sender_full_name": "Syed Shaazib Tanvir",
        "timestamp": 1772976789
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Just use the range syntax, <code>arr[start...stop]</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subarray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ys</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subarray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">3.</span><span class=\"bp\">..</span><span class=\"m\">10</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subarray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ys</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">2.</span><span class=\"bp\">..</span><span class=\"m\">5</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">zs</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 578009090,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1772977247
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks, I was initially trying the xs[a:b] syntax.<br>\nIs there a reason why arrays also don't use the xs[a...b] syntax for uniformity?</p>",
        "id": 578010526,
        "sender_full_name": "Syed Shaazib Tanvir",
        "timestamp": 1772977530
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>They do though?</p>",
        "id": 578011281,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1772977780
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>xs[a:b]</code> is legacy syntax</p>",
        "id": 578011309,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1772977789
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/CHFEWxAqk8OU5AEQVVfsHhoQ/image.png\">image.png</a><br>\noh, I'm guessing docs aren't updated to warn that it's deprecated</p>\n<div class=\"message_inline_image\"><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/CHFEWxAqk8OU5AEQVVfsHhoQ/image.png\" title=\"image.png\"><img data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"1048x845\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/CHFEWxAqk8OU5AEQVVfsHhoQ/image.png/840x560.webp\"></a></div>",
